Description: Keep your Flatpak apps updated from the system tray
 Flatpak Manager watches the Flatpak apps you choose to track. A green
 arrow in the system tray means everything is up to date; a gold arrow
 means updates are waiting.
 .
 Select several apps and update them together, search Flathub and install
 apps, open Flathub install links and .flatpakref files, and run routine
 maintenance (remove unused runtimes, repair, refresh) in a few clicks.
 .
 Free to use on up to 10 installations at the same time; more than that
 needs a paid license (see /usr/share/doc/flatpak-manager/LICENSE.txt).

